{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "aizuchi",
  "title": "Reactions & Listening",
  "order": 12,
  "description": "The small words that show you’re listening and react to what you hear. They keep a Japanese conversation going.",
  "phrases": [
    {
      "id": "aiz-01",
      "register": "casual",
      "japanese": "そうなんだ",
      "furigana": [
        {
          "b": "そうなんだ"
        }
      ],
      "romaji": "sō nanda",
      "english": "Oh, really? / I see.",
      "polite": {
        "japanese": "そうなんですか",
        "furigana": [
          {
            "b": "そうなんですか"
          }
        ],
        "romaji": "sō nan desu ka",
        "audio": "audio/ja/aiz-01-polite.mp3"
      },
      "registerNotes": "The all-purpose “oh, is that so”: it shows you’ve taken in something new. Let it rise a little; said flat, it sounds bored.",
      "audio": "audio/ja/aiz-01.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "reaction",
        "essential"
      ],
      "difficulty": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "aiz-02",
      "japanese": "なるほど",
      "furigana": [
        {
          "b": "なるほど"
        }
      ],
      "romaji": "naruhodo",
      "english": "I see. / That makes sense.",
      "registerNotes": "For when something’s been explained. To someone above you, なるほど alone can sound like you’re grading their answer; そうなんですね is safer.",
      "audio": "audio/ja/aiz-02.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "reaction",
        "essential"
      ],
      "difficulty": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "aiz-03",
      "register": "casual",
      "japanese": "へえ、すごい",
      "furigana": [
        {
          "b": "へえ、すごい"
        }
      ],
      "romaji": "hē, sugoi",
      "english": "Wow, that’s amazing.",
      "polite": {
        "japanese": "へえ、すごいですね",
        "furigana": [
          {
            "b": "へえ、すごいですね"
          }
        ],
        "romaji": "hē, sugoi desu ne",
        "audio": "audio/ja/aiz-03-polite.mp3"
      },
      "registerNotes": "Real interest, out loud. The long へえ does half the work: Japanese listeners expect to hear you react.",
      "audio": "audio/ja/aiz-03.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "reaction"
      ],
      "difficulty": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "aiz-04",
      "register": "casual",
      "japanese": "それで？",
      "furigana": [
        {
          "b": "それで？"
        }
      ],
      "romaji": "sorede?",
      "english": "And then?",
      "polite": {
        "japanese": "それで、どうなったんですか",
        "furigana": [
          {
            "b": "それで、どうなったんですか"
          }
        ],
        "romaji": "sorede, dō natta n desu ka?",
        "audio": "audio/ja/aiz-04-polite.mp3"
      },
      "registerNotes": "Asks them to carry on with the story, and shows you want to hear it.",
      "audio": "audio/ja/aiz-04.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "listening"
      ],
      "difficulty": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "aiz-05",
      "register": "casual",
      "japanese": "わかる",
      "furigana": [
        {
          "b": "わかる"
        }
      ],
      "romaji": "wakaru",
      "english": "I know what you mean.",
      "polite": {
        "japanese": "わかります",
        "furigana": [
          {
            "b": "わかります"
          }
        ],
        "romaji": "wakarimasu",
        "audio": "audio/ja/aiz-05-polite.mp3"
      },
      "registerNotes": "Sympathy, not just understanding: わかる！ is “I know, right?”. The polite わかります works the same way.",
      "audio": "audio/ja/aiz-05.mp3",
      "tags": [
        "reaction",
        "agreeing"
      ],
      "difficulty": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "aiz-06",
